%% effects-scheduling: when UseEffect runs relative to render + commit.
%% Reads: Render -> Reconciler.Mount/Update -> WinUI tree visible
%% -> FlushEffects (cleanup-of-prev THEN run-new).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Component.Render
    participant R as Reconciler
    participant U as WinUI tree
    participant E as ctx.FlushEffects
    C->>R: returns Element tree
    R->>R: diff old vs new
    R->>U: mount / update controls (commit)
    Note over U: pixels visible to user
    R->>E: FlushEffectsTraced(ctx)
    E->>E: phase 1 — run pending cleanups (prev deps)
    E->>E: phase 2 — run new effect bodies
    Note over E: setState here<br/>schedules another render
